{{Documentation/Header}}
Normalizes a page name into the full title that transcluding it would resolve to. A bare name such as <code>Foo</code> becomes <code>Template:Foo</code>; a colon-prefixed name such as <code>:Foo</code> becomes the article <code>Foo</code>; a name that already carries a namespace is returned unchanged.

Used by link and demo templates that need to display or link to whatever a given transclusion actually points at.

==Syntax==
{{T|Transclude|v1=page name}}

==Examples==
{| class="dataTable"
! Input !! Result
|-
| <code>Foo</code> || <code>Template:Foo</code>
|-
| <code>:Foo</code> || <code>Foo</code>
|-
| <code>Help:Foo</code> || <code>Help:Foo</code>
|}

{| class="dataTable sortable"
! Parameter !! Aliases !! Label !! Description !! Type !! Default !! Status
|-
| <code>1</code> || – || Page name || The page name to normalize. || string || – || <span style="color:red;font-weight:bold;">Required</span>
|}